<header><h1>The L1Z1X Mindnet</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="assimilate"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Assimilate">Assimilate</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any space docks that are placed by this ability during a tactical action may produce units during the <b>Production</b> step of that tactical action.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player resolves their <sc>Assimilate</sc> ability, and then plays the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Infiltrate"><i>Infiltrate</i></a> action card, or vice versa, they will replace zero PDS and space docks with zero PDS and space docks when they resolve the latter ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player would have to place a structure, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may, but are not required to, remove a structure of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead.<sup>1,2,4</sup></li>
    <li>When the L1Z1X player gains control of a planet, they also replace coexisting structures on that planet.<sup>6</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="harrow"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow">Harrow</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a> ability will prevent the use of the <sc>Harrow</sc> ability on a planet.<sup>1,2,3</sup></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player cannot use their <sc>Harrow</sc> ability if they are not the active player.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player may use their <sc>Harrow</sc> ability at the end of the round in which their last ground force was destroyed. This may cause the combat to end in a draw.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>Every unit in the active system with the <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> ability may use it against the planet the ground combat is taking place on, regardless of whether that unit bombarded that planet during the <b>Bombardment</b> step of the invasion.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <ol><li>An Annihilator may bombard when using <sc>Harrow</sc> if that mech is not currently participating in ground combat, even if it has been committed to a different planet, and has been or will be involved in another ground combat during the current invasion.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The L1Z1X player may use the ability of the <span class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon"><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</i></a></span> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon"><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;&Omega;</i></a> technologies whenever they bombard.<sup>10,15</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="cybernetic-enhancements" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Cybernetic%20Enhancements">Cybernetic Enhancements</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>10</sup></li>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player has no command tokens in their strategy pool, <i>Cybernetic Enhancements</i> cannot be played.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="cybernetic-enhancements-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Cybernetic%20Enhancements">Cybernetic Enhancements &Omega;</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="inheritance-systems"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Inheritance%20Systems">Inheritance Systems</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The two resources for <i>Inheritance Systems</i> must be paid in addition to and separately from any other costs paid to research the technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>For example, if the L1Z1X player is performing the secondary of the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card, they cannot spend the five resources of [0.0.0] plus one trade good to pay for the costs of both <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> and <i>Inheritance Systems</i>. Instead, they would have to spend [0.0.0] to pay for the cost of <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a>, wasting the fifth resource, then spend two additional resources to pay for the cost of <i>Inheritance Systems</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>The owner of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Sciences"><i>Minister of Sciences</i></a> law must still spend the two resources for <i>Inheritance Systems</i>, as they pay to ignore prerequisites, not to research the technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li><i>Inheritance Systems</i> may be used when researching a unit upgrade technology, including the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s own faction technologies such as <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Dreadnought:~:text=Super-Dreadnought">Super Dreadnought</a> II.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If <i>Inheritance Systems</i> is researched as the first of two technologies researched back to back, such as with the primary ability of the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Ixthian%20Artifact"><i>Ixthian Artifact</i></a> agenda, it may be used immediately to ignore the prerequisites of the second technology.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="super-dreadnought"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Dreadnought:~:text=Super-Dreadnought">Super Dreadnought</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="0-0-1"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Flagship:~:text=%5B0.0.1%5D">[0.0.1]</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="i48s"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=I48S">I48S</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The infantry must be in the system when it is activated for it to be eligible to be replaced. It cannot be replaced if it is moved into or produced in the active system later in the turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="2ram"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=2RAM">2RAM</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Those units still have <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li class="removed">The player that owns those units may still use the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid"><i>Magen Defense Grid</i></a> technology.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-helmsman"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=The%20Helmsman">The Helmsman</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=Dark%20Space%20Navigation">Dark Space Navigation</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Ships in systems with one of the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens may move.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>When the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s ships move outside of a tactical action, they may transport units from systems that contain the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Ships move directly to their destination system. They may only transport units from their origin system.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Ships moving out of a gravity rift must roll for removal.<sup>1,2,3,4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Ships do not roll for removal if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_IV:~:text=Circlet%20of%20the%20Void"><i>Circlet of the Void</i></a> relic.<sup>11</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Ships cannot move into a supernova, even with <i>Dark Space Navigation</i>.<sup>1,2,3</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Ships may move into a supernova if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_IV:~:text=Circlet%20of%20the%20Void"><i>Circlet of the Void</i></a> relic.<sup>11</sup></li>
        <li>Ships may travel into an asteroid field only if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li><i>Dark Space Navigation</i> may be used to move ships into the wormhole nexus. If the nexus is inactive, this will cause it to activate.<sup>1,8</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="annihilator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Mech:~:text=Annihilator">Annihilator</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>An Annihilator may bombard when using the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> ability if that mech is not currently participating in ground combat, even if it has been committed to a different planet, and has been or will be involved in another ground combat during the current invasion.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="fealty-uplink"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Breakthrough:~:text=Fealty%20Uplink">Fealty Uplink</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the L1Z1X player gains control of an uncontrolled planet, they may choose if they place the infantry before or after they explore the planet.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player must mandatorily place the infantry.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
